    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "This occurs because `_list_with_default` that uses the values of `input.size()` as defaults for positions where `output_size` is None is called before the call to the aten adaptive_avg_pool2d [which checks whether `output_size` is 2d].(https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/main/aten/src/ATen/native/AdaptiveAveragePooling.cpp#L30) \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/f8aedf1efedc04bde6e27a1ccd64b08fc38ae56b/torch/nn/functional.py#L1231-L1232\r\n\r\nI suppose it might be reasonable to check the dimensionality of `output_size` before passing to `_list_with_default` ",
